 "_note": "Hand-authored fixture (edit directly, then `pnpm --filter @oybc/shared run gen:sync-fixtures`). Pins packages/shared/src/algorithms/boardMoment.ts (tests/algorithms/boardMoment.test.ts) against its Swift twin Helpers/BoardMoment.swift (OYBCTests/BoardMomentVectorTests.swift) - docs/BOARD_MOMENTS.md. Each case is `{name, board, tasks, children?, boardTasks, allBoards?, events, expected, frames}`. Defaults for unlisted fields: Task type=normal, isCompleted=false, isDeleted=false, createdAt=2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z, title=id; Event kind=increment when `delta` is set else completion, id=`e<index>`, isDeleted=false; Board status=active, timeframe=custom, totalTasks=size*size, linesCompleted=len(completedLineIds); placements isDeleted=false, boardId=board.id; links isDeleted=false. `board` = {id, size, centerSquareType, startDate, endDate, completedTasks, completedLineIds?, sealedAt?, sealedCompletedCells?, status?}; `allBoards` entries use the same shape (size 3, centre free) and feed ACHIEVEMENT cells only; `tasks[].referencedBoardId` / `achievementTrigger` configure an achievement. The test calls computeBoardMomentReplay(board, boardTasks, childrenByCompound, taskById, eventsByTaskId, allBoards) with events grouped by taskId (a sealed board is bounded at sealedAt inside the kernel) and compares `expected` = {order[{boardTaskId, idx, completedAt}], freeIdx, lineClosureBeat{lineId: beat}, completedTasks, totalTasks, size, finalBeat{bingo, greenlog}} (finalBeat = momentFinalBeat(replay, kind)). Beats: beat 0 = empty board; order[i] lands at beat i+1; a line closes at max(land beat of its non-FREE cells)+1; a greenlog wave reaches cell (r,c) at order.length+1+r+c; lines never flip during a greenlog's landing pass. Each `frames` entry = {kind, beat, counter, landed[idx], green[idx], popTokens{idx: token}}: counter = momentCounterAt(beat) = max(0, completedTasks - order.length + min(beat, order.length)); landed/green/popTokens come from momentCellVisual(idx, beat, replay, kind) for every idx (a cell is listed under landed/green only when true; popTokens omits null; popToken = the cell's green beat when green, else its land beat when landed, else null; the FREE centre is never `landed`). Cases: simple cells in shuffled completion order with two lines closing on the 3rd and 5th squares and a FREE centre (in its lines, never in the closure max); a counting cell whose crossing increment (08:30) is earlier than its last log (12:00); a compound whose completing child is the last of all-of; a completed ACHIEVEMENT cell (no instant) sorting after every dated cell; a 4x4 with no FREE and two lines closing at different beats; a greenlog with two squares at the same instant (tie by idx) and every line present; a sealed board whose sealedCompletedCells disagrees with live events (the sealed set wins, a post-seal event is bounded out).",
